# Documentation: 04-settings.http REST client collection.
# - Exercises tenant settings retrieval/update plus the CRUD flow for extra tenant charges.
# - Use an admin token for write requests because the charge catalog drives downstream payment behavior.
# - These requests are written for the VS Code REST Client extension and use its response-variable syntax extensively.
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8787
@json = application/json
@seedPassword = Test@1234
@tenantId = tenant_0001
@adminEmail = admin.seed-gym-1@seed.gym.test

# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin.seed-gym-1@seed.gym.test",
  "password": "Test@1234"
}

### Get tenant settings
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}

### Update tenant settings
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "overdueDays": 21
}

### List charges
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/charges
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}

### Create a charge
# @name createCharge
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/charges
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "REST Client Charge {{$timestamp}}",
  "amount": 75000,
  "isMandatory": false
}

### Update the new charge
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/charges/{{createCharge.response.body.$.data.charge.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 65000,
  "isActive": true
}

### Delete the new charge
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/charges/{{createCharge.response.body.$.data.charge.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
